  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Republic of Congo Third Fiscal Management and Inclusive Growth DPF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program Development Objective is to support the government&apos;s efforts to: (i) strengthen revenue mobilization and public financial management; and (ii) improve the conditions for inclusive and sustainable growth.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Third Fiscal Management and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Financing Program is to support the government&apos;s efforts to: (i) strengthen revenue mobilization and public financial management; and (ii) improve the conditions for inclusive and sustainable growth. This Third Fiscal Management and Inclusive Growth Development Policy Financing (DPF) is the final operation in a programmatic series and will be financed by an IDA credit of 61.1 million dollars equivalent and an IBRD loan of 18.9 million dollars. It supports the government&apos;s efforts to strengthen revenue mobilization and public financial management (PFM) and improve the conditions for inclusive and sustainable growth. The first pillar of the proposed DPF supports reforms to strengthen revenue mobilization from both the oil and non-oil sectors and PFM. The second pillar supports reforms critical for economic diversification and inclusion, including competition, business environment, human capital, protection of the most vulnerable populations, and access to electricity. The reforms supported are complementary to World Bank- Investment and Program-for-Results (PforR) operations; and build on the World Bank&apos;s core analytics, notably the recent Country Economic Memorandum, Public Finance Review, Country Climate and Development Report, and Public Expenditure and Financial Accountability assessment. The DPF series also complements the recently completed International Monetary Fund (IMF) three-year Extended Credit Facility (ECF) program.</narrative>
  </description>
